{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774474583,"nonce":"H/TRM1IvyVVIcS7L2dCNxx/Apn8=","message":"💭 Now I understand the bug. The watcher loop runs `check_reviewer_done()` before `check_orphaned_sessions()`. When a review session completes successfully (status `waiting:review`, container exits), `check_reviewer_done` tries to extract a verdict. If it can't find one immediately, it returns. Then `check_orphaned_sessions` sees `waiting:review` + no container for the review session and misclassifies it as an orphan (lines 90-91). The review gets restarted, completes again, same thing repeats → hits MAX_ORPHAN_RESUMES → suspended:review-failed.","files":null}]}